Ok, it's taken forever but my weird conduct tourist is finally filling
himself full of !oBooze in the Demigod Bar.  Allow me to introduce
Hall the Atheist Wishless Genoless Extinctionist!

Just to clear up any doubt, here's what I mean by extinctionist: Hall
killed every monster that was generated by the game or that could be
generated by create monster spells except for a few notable exceptions
(see below).  He did not use reverse genocide - only a bag of tricks,
scrolls and wands of create monster, and other monster's summon
spells.

Creatures left alive were - Izchak, the peaceful inhabitants of
Ankh-Morpork, a few sea creatures on the plane of water (he really
couldn't be bothered if they weren't extinctable or summonable), and a
few priests on the astral plane (again, they can't be summoned or
extincted so he lost interest).  Apart from these, the dungeons and
the planes will be empty forever.  Oh, and he forgot Demogorgon
(Doh!).

This is my third ascension (excluding one Valk in celestial disgrace
and one death on the Astral Plane) and my first conduct ascension. 
The notes are sketchy in places - extinctionist takes a long, long
time and the beginning of the game was quite some time ago.  Apologies
also for the length of this post.

I doubt I will ever do another extinctionist, but I'd say it was
certainly worth it, just this once, in order to have the experience of
walking through the dungeon and the elemental planes while they were
(almost) totally deserted.  And to see messages like "The priest casts
a spell at a bunch of sticks, but nothing happens".  I very much
enjoyed atheist conduct - it added a huge challenge to the game which
needed a lot of thought to get around.  I'll certainly start on
another conduct ascension soon.

SPOILERS AHEAD!!!

--The Story--

Hall the Tourist was always going to be an atheist - he didn't believe
in the pagan gods that were worthipped by the denizens of the Dungeons
of Doom.  As such, he had a number of interesting problems which
needed to be overcome.  Finding holy water, finding a decent artefact
weapon, and getting together a decent set of armour are all things
that become more of a challenge for an atheist.  He also found that he
had to rely a lot more on his pet to test the b/u/c status of objects.

Level 1 contained a sink and not much else of interest.  He had a
stroke of luck when level 2 turned out to have a ring superstore.  He
stole a bunch of rings and took them upstairs to drop then down the
sink.  He ended up with poly control, free action, slow digestion,
levitation, invis, and a few others.

On level 3 he found an armour shop.  He stole lots of un-id'd armour,
some elven mithril, a cloak of displacement and a cloak of
invisibility.

He then decided to go to minetown, instead of going to Sokoban as most
of his predecessors had done.  It turned out to be a good trip, and he
came back with three pets (a forest centaur, a warhorse and a large
cat), a bag of holding, a wand of poly, AC-5, HP 83 and already
character level 9.

He then went to Sokoban and liberated the amulet.

Then Hall decided to go and look for a luckstone that the shopkeepers
in minetown had been talking about.  He went down to Mine's End and
found it near a wine cellar.  He got a little bit grumpy at Mine's End
because he was carrying around so much unidentified stuff.  In a fit
of impatience he read some of his scrolls to identify them.  Luckily,
one of them turned out to be identify.  He identified some of the
stuff from the armour shop and the ornamental cope turned out to be a
+1 Cloak of Magic Resistance!

After Mine's End he went down to find the quest with his pet marilith
and pet aleax.  Unfortunately, Twoflower said that he wasn't
experienced enough to do quest so he explored down to Medusa instead.

When he came back he still wasn't experienced enough to do the quest,
so he found Fort Ludios and killed some dragons there to see if he
could use their hides to make armour.  Only the white one left scales,
so made some WDSM.  Although there was a castle in Fort Ludios he
decided not to attempt it until he was stronger.  There were 5 more
dragons in there including a gray one, but he only had a runed dagger,
and had not yet seen a scroll of enchant weapon, so he decided not to
risk it.

Hall then spent some time wandering around the dungeon aimlessly
killing things to try and gain experience.  At some point his aleax
hit a trap and was polymorphed into a pit fiend.  Somewhere around
level 18 Hall ate a tengu corpse and got teleport control, but he
didn't have the ability to teleport yet.  He finally found a silver
saber on level 20 when a captain dropped one.  He found his first
scroll of enchant weapon on level 22, and used it to enchant the
silver saber.

He stopped at level 23, as there was a mind flayer there and didn't
want to tangle with it yet.  He went back up to level 20 and hung
around killing things in order to gain experience for the quest.  He
met an Aleax who dropped a polished silver shield.  Unfortunately,
carrying it around made him very stressed, but when he dropped his
thoroughly rusty corroded +1 dwarvish helm that made it better.

At this point in the game Hall's key problems were (i) lack of holy
water (he had only seen two scrolls of remove curse this game and
neither had yielded the desired result), (ii) lack of scrolls of
enchant weapon, (iii) paucity of armour, and (iv) lack of experience.

In order to try and remedy these problems, he headed back up to level
15 and hung around killing things for a while.  During this killfest
he got sleep resistance from a grey-elf, and got speed from a quantum
mechanic corpse.

He finally got up to character level 14 the hard way, and went back to
see Twoflower.  He found gauntlets of power on the third level of the
quest (in the town).  He spent a long time on that level identifying
things.  Getting impatient again, he quaffed an unidentified potion
and it turned out to by polymorph.  He ripped out of his CoMR and
T-Shirt, which proved to be a bit of a set-back.  When he was back to
normal shape he tamed a warhorse, and used a polymorph trap on the
level below to turn it into a titan.

On the bottom on the quest Hall found a potion of water which didn't
stack with the others he was carrying.  He dipped two potions of
uncursed water into it and they glowed light blue.  Holy water -
finally!!  He spent some time blessing and uncursing objects and then
completed the quest.

He now felt that he was prepared to go to Fort Ludios again.  He knew
there was a gray dragon in there, and he desperately needed magic
resistance (having forgotten temporarily that the PYEC provided him
with it).  He did some alchemy first, and felt safer after quaffing 12
blessed diluted potions of full healing.  He polymorphed a pile of
unicorn horns and got a magic marker.  He used this to get his AC down
to -21, his silver saber to +7 and his 11 blessed daggers to +5.

Hall then defeated Croesus and killed the gray dragon, but it didn't
leave scales.  The white dragon in the fort did leave him another set
of white scales though.  He raised his eyes and gave thanks to the
RNG, the one true god.  He identified the plumed helmet he'd been
wearing and found it was a helm of brilliance.  He then decided to go
back up through the dungeon learning spellbooks to see if he could
find either identify or create monster.

He ate a leprechaun at mine's end and finally gained the ability to
teleport.  He found a spellbook of create monster but not identify, so
he continued descending to medusa.

He stopped on level 19 for a long time having a killfest in order to
build up some nice equipment.  He used the PYEC to recharge bag of
tricks and several wands of create monster.  There was no particular
reason for this - it was simply something to do.  After a long time he
decided to become an extinctionist and moved up to level 1 to continue
killing.  He used his bag of tricks, and whenever a monster dropped a
wand of create monster he used all the charges except one before
snapping it in half.

A long time passed.

Turn 366,081: Hall applied the bag of tricks on dlvl 1 and nothing
came out.  By this point he had AC -32 (all armour at +5 except gloves
of power at +4) and 3034 HP.  He had swapped his WDSM for some YDSM. 
He zapped the 4:4 /oPoly at the final pile of magical tools and got a
few more magic markers and a figurine of an Archon.  He blessed and
applied the figurine and got a hostile Archon.  Unfortunately he
couldn't tame it and so had to put it out of his misery.  He then
enchanted Demonbane up to +7, #twoweaponed it with a +8 silver sabre
and headed downstairs.  His plan was to move progressively through
each level, clearing all monsters and applying his trusty bag of
tricks until no more monsters were generated.

He descended through the mines, stopping on each level to extinct any
monsters that could be summoned before moving on.  He paused for a
while in minetown to extinct ghosts at the altar room.  He decided to
leave Izchak alive.

He also left a gray unicorn on level 8 of main dungeon so that he
could control his luck.

By the time Hall got down to Medusa Archons had been extincted (2
levels above Medusa).  Medusa's level was silent apart from sea
creatures (not extinctable).  There were 2 levels of mazes, then an
empty castle apart from 2 liches and 2 disenchanters.  The VOTD was
full of demons, ghosts and wraiths.  He stopped at the entrance to the
VOTD and extincted all demons, the two remaining flavours of lich,
green slimes and disenchanters.  The disenchanters ruined his +8
saber, and disenchanted his armour down to +16.  He disenchanted them
permanently with his pick-axe.  A quick trip up to the main stash on
level 1 remedied the damage to the armour, but not the saber.

The fight in the VOTD saw the deaths of Yeenoghu and Jubilex, who were
summoned by liches.  It was probably the hardest fight of the game -
the combination of Master Liches, Archliches and Disenchanters in
large numbers (due to breaking wands of create monster and reading
cursed scrolls of create monster) meant that it was not unsual to lose
1000 hp in a battle.

At turn 453,022 Hall entered Gehennom.  There were no monsters on the
first level - only the Minotaur that owned the maze.

He spent some time communing with Asmodeus in order to kill erinyes,
barbed devils and horned devils.  Asmodeus summoned Baalzebub.  Hall
parked on the stairs, blindfolded himself to avoid Baalzebub's stun
attacks, and extincted the remaining demons.  Baalzebub was helpful
enough to summon Dispater, who in turn summoned Geryon.

Hall hung around with Orcus for a while to try and get him to summon
Demogorgon.  Unfortunately Orcus summoned a black dragon which
promptly disintegrated him!  Hall laughed so hard that he had to sit
down for a while.

He then descended to the bottom of Gehennom, found the VS, and
surrounded it with rocks to mark it.  At this point the only things
alive in the dungeon were Izchak, Rodney, the gray unicorn on level 8,
Twoflower and the friendly guides in Ankh-Morpork.  He went up to his
level 1 stash and sorted out his final ascension kit.  He swapped
gauntlets of power for gauntlets of dexterity and learned cure
sickness at 0% - he'd heard rumour that one of his predecessors had
been killed by a Rider called Pestillence.  He also swapped his +7
Demonbane for a +7 Frostbrand which he'd found during his killfest on
level 1.  He picked up 22 cursed !oGL and went downstairs to kill
Rodney.

Rodney was no trouble at all.  Hall went back down to the VS after the
battle and performed the invocation.  The Sanctum was almost
completely empty apart from a few wraiths and some priests and
priestesses.  He found the door to the temple using the Bell of
Opening and killed the high priest.  He grabbed the amulet and started
to ascend through the dungeon.  He had heard rumours that he would be
dragged downstairs by a mysterious force, but it didn't seem as bad as
he'd been led to believe.  He only got pulled back 7 or 8 times in the
end.  When he got to level 8 he tossed some gems to the unicorn to
boost his luck and then killed it.  On level 2 he remembered the pile
of c!oGL that he'd been lugging around.  He shrugged, dropped them and
moved on.  He then went up to stash and made sure he had all that he
would need for the Elemental Planes.  Just to be sure he re-read the
spellbooks of identify and cure sickness.  He picked up the bag of
holding named "treasure" and discovered that he was so stressed that
he couldn't climb the stairs out of the dungeon.  He had to leave 150k
gold behind on the stairs up from dungeon level 1 in the end.
 
He went up the stairs to the plane of earth.  The only things left
alive in the dungeon were Izchak, and his friends in Ankh-Morpork.  A
minotaur was on the plane of earth, and Rodney appeared twice.  Three
djinni were on the plane of air.  Rodney appeared again on the plane
of fire, along with another minotaur.  A few sea creatures were
paddling about on the plane of water.  The planes went by very fast
due to confused ?oGD.  Hall found the portal on the plane of water and
saved standing next to it.  The savefile went from 1.32Mb to 38k.

After a break he came back to do the Astral plane.  Just after he
stepped through the portal to the Astral Plane Hall remembered that
he'd forgotten to persuade Rodney to sumon Demogorgon, so he kicked
himself very hard.  Wrapping his towel around his head he saw that
Pestillence was on the left, in the middle was Famine, and to the
right was Death.  He decided to killed each rider at least once
(Pestillence, then Famine, then Death), and then headed back to the
central altar to ascend.  Death drained his HP from 5766 to 5692.  On
the way back to the central altar he killed Eve the Nomad, who kindly
dropped Magicbane.  He paused and gave thanks to the RNG for giving
him this most useful  of boons at such an appropriate time.  He killed
Famine a few times, more to make a point than anything else, and then
ascended.

